### **Problems/Challenges/Roadblocks (specify “resolved/not resolved” status)**

1. **Authentication/login issue – status: not resolved.** While testing the feature manually through the browser, I found that the existing `/login/` page did not complete the login process, which prevented me from reaching the Tasks page through the normal browser login flow. I reviewed the existing authentication code and confirmed that the issue was related to the existing login implementation rather than the Card 3.3 task-editing changes. Because authentication was outside the scope of Card 3.3, I did not modify the login functionality. Instead, I used Django's automated test client to authenticate test users directly and verify the Card 3.3 functionality. The automated tests successfully confirmed that authenticated users can edit their own tasks, status changes persist, and users cannot edit another user's tasks. The complete project test suite passed with **14 tests and 0 failures**.

2. **Form and view implementation issues – status: resolved.** During development, I worked through implementation and indentation issues in the task view and corrected them before running the tests.

3. **User-data access protection – status: resolved.** I verified that the edit view checks both the task ID and the logged-in user, preventing users from editing another user's task. The authorization test passed successfully.